Description: ChIPpeakAnno is a comprehensive Bioconductor package for batch
    annotation and analysis of peaks from ChIP-seq, ATAC-seq, CUT&RUN,
    CUT&Tag, CLIP-seq, and other genomic interval experiments. The package
    provides a systematic workflow from quality assessment through annotation
    to downstream enrichment analysis. Key capabilities include: (1) quality
    assessment and filtering of peaks per replicate, (2) consensus peak
    creation from multiple replicates using IDR or overlap-based methods, (3)
    factor-specific hierarchical annotation with intelligent prioritization
    strategies for transcription factors, histone marks, and other factor
    types, (4) integration with epigenomic databases including ENCODE cCREs
    and Roadmap Epigenomics with automatic liftOver support, (5) enhancer
    identification using Hi-C data, ENCODE CRE annotations, and Epigenetics
    Roadmap enhancer annotations, (6) enrichment analysis for gene ontology
    (GO)/pathways using databases such as MSigDB and EnrichR, (7) sequence
    extraction for motif discovery compatible with external tools (HOMER,
    STREME, FIMO) and R packages (memes, monaLisa) for in-depth motif
    analysis, (8) visualization tools including metagene plots,
    feature-aligned heatmaps, and signal profiles, and (9) statistical
    testing for peak overlaps and enrichment. The package supports multiple
    annotation sources (TxDb, EnsDb, biomaRt, custom GRanges) and provides
    unique functions for identifying peaks near bi-directional promoters. It
    integrates seamlessly with the Bioconductor ecosystem including
    GenomicRanges, Biostrings, BSgenome, and annotation databases.
